25, este organismo adjudicó 102 contratos menores de servicios y suministros de más de 14.000 y hasta 15.000 euros, justo por debajo del límite legal. Si esos importes se repartieran como en la franja inmediatamente inferior, lo esperable serían 14,4 contratos. La razón entre observados y esperados es 7,1, con un intervalo de confianza del 95 % de 5,2 a 9,7. En diciembre se adjudicó el 14 % de los contratos junto al límite, mientras que diciembre supone el 11 % de todos sus contratos de servicios y suministros. Los contratos junto al límite se reparten entre 73 adjudicatarios distintos. El contrato [1], de 14.965 euros, se adjudicó en diciembre de 2025.\nQué no pueden demostrar: La concentración de contratos al límite no indica malas prácticas. Puede deberse a factores como precios de mercado o necesidades específicas. No hay datos que confirman irregularidades.\nQué se puede revisar: Comprobar si los contratos [1] y [2] atienden la misma necesidad. Verificar si el adjudicatario A repite contratos en otros áreas. Analizar si los contratos al límite coinciden con presupuestos cerrados o necesidades urgentes.","en":"What the data shows: Between 2023 and 2025, this body awarded 102 minor contracts for services and supplies above 14,000 and up to 15,000 euros, just under the legal limit. If those amounts were spread as in the band immediately below, 14.4 contracts would be expected. The observed-to-expected ratio is 7.1, with a 95% confidence interval of 5.2 to 9.7. December accounts for 14% of the contracts just under the limit, compared with 11% of all its services and supplies contracts. The awardee with the most contracts just under the limit, called awardee A here, has 5. Contract [1], for 14,965 euros, was awarded in December 2025.\nWhat it cannot show: The concentration of contracts in December and the high number of unique awardees do not indicate improper conduct. These patterns could reflect market conditions, budget constraints, or operational needs, not wrongdoing.\nWhat can be checked: Check the distribution of contracts by month and awardee to identify unusual patterns. Review contract details, such as the goods and services provided, to ensure they align with the body's stated objectives. Examine if multiple contracts cover the same need to assess potential overlap or redundancy.","origen_es":"modelo","origen_en":"modelo","modelo":"Qwen3-4B (Q4_K_M, llama.cpp)","regla":"ss","citas":["6k1Gfo9ZvhZ9Zh%2FyRJgM8w%3D%3D","WTPfSi4GS6bkY6rls5tG9A%3D%3D","HBiZXz%2F9Jn8ZDGvgaZEVxQ%3D%3D"],"generado":"2026-11-15"}}